{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/d6q3a2","slideIndex":0,"text":"Layered architecture inside the ESP32-C6. The application uses NimBLE host APIs. The host includes GAP, GATT/ATT, SMP and L2CAP. The HCI/VHCI boundary connects the host with the Espressif Bluetooth controller. The controller includes Link Layer functions and PHY support. The PHY/radio is shown as the hardware-facing layer, not a separate external microcontroller. Bidirectional arrows represent commands, events and BLE data. Firmware sources: esp32/components/ble/ble.c, ble_gap.c, ble_gatt.c; sdkconfig confirms esp32c6, NimBLE host and enabled Bluetooth controller. Official references: https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32c6/api-reference/bluetooth/nimble/index.html and https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/stable/esp32c6/api-guides/ble/get-started/ble-introduction.html"}